I got it working, I don't know much about this stuff, so I'm not sure if this is the best way to solve it, but it does work at least, should I create a PR?

This is the commit with the working solution, it might be hacky though, not sure if that's the correct way of handling it.
https://github.com/DanielSnd/godot/commit/d4d99d099cf06338b1ef0bae5dd289bc97b747fd

For updating the existing textures I found that they there was a LocalVector with their RIDs I could access in texturestorage so I created a method to update all of them:


```cpp
void TextureStorage::update_all_texture_lod_bias() {
    Config *config = Config::get_singleton();
	if (config == nullptr) {
		return;
	}

    float texture_mipmap_bias = config->texture_mipmap_bias;
    for (const RID &rid : texture_owner.get_owned_list()) {
		Texture *texture = texture_owner.get_or_null(rid);

        if (!texture || !texture->active || texture->tex_id == 0) {
            continue;
        }

        glActiveTexture(GL_TEXTURE0);
        glBindTexture(texture->target, texture->tex_id);

        if (texture->mipmaps > 1 && texture_mipmap_bias != 0.0f) {
            glTexParameterf(texture->target, GL_TEXTURE_LOD_BIAS, texture_mipmap_bias);
        } else if (texture_mipmap_bias == 0.0f) {
            // Reset to 0 if bias is disabled
            glTexParameterf(texture->target, GL_TEXTURE_LOD_BIAS, 0.0f);
        }
	}

    glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0);
}
```


